  "id": "grammar.a1.76.a",
  "title": "Hány óra van? - Whole hours",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Explanation",
      "content": "To ask the time, say *Hány óra van?* (word for word “how many hours is it?”). To answer a whole hour, put the number before *óra*: *Három óra van.* “It is three o’clock.” *Óra* stays singular after a number. You know the numbers up to ten. Two small changes: *kettő* (two) shortens to *két* before a noun, so *Két óra van.*, and the last two hours are *tizenegy* (eleven) and *tizenkettő* (twelve), which also shortens before *óra*: *Tizenkét óra van.*"
    },
